{
  "id": "poisson_s_ratio___definition__values_for_materials",
  "title": "Poisson's Ratio Calculator",
  "description": "Calculate Poisson's ratio from strain measurements and explore Poisson's ratio values for common materials. Poisson's ratio describes the relationship between transverse strain and longitudinal strain when a material is deformed.",
  "type": "calculator",
  "components": [
    {
      "type": "markdown",
      "content": "## Poisson's Ratio Calculator\n\nPoisson's ratio (μ) is the ratio of transverse strain to longitudinal strain when a material is deformed:\n\n**μ = - εt / εl**\n\nWhere:\n- εt = transverse strain (lateral contraction)\n- εl = longitudinal strain (axial extension)\n\nFor most common materials, Poisson's ratio ranges from 0 to 0.5.",
      "headers": []
    },
    {
      "type": "calculator",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "id": "transverse_strain",
          "label": "Transverse Strain (εt)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 0.001,
          "unit": "m/m"
        },
        {
          "id": "longitudinal_strain",
          "label": "Longitudinal Strain (εl)",
          "type": "number",
          "defaultValue": 0.003,
          "unit": "m/m"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "id": "poisson_ratio",
          "label": "Poisson's Ratio (μ)",
          "formula": "-(inputs.transverse_strain / inputs.longitudinal_strain)",
          "format": "decimal",
          "unit": "dimensionless"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
